  "name": "XDK sell-recycle moves XDK out of its own pair",
  "summary": "On every sell into its main pair, XDK's _recycleFromBlackHoleOnSell() moves up to 10% of the sell amount, plus a proportional share, of XDK straight out of the XDK/GPC pair to the dead address and to the token, then syncs the pair, capped only at 10% of the pair's XDK per day. Inside a GPC flash swap from the WBNB/GPC pair, the attacker bought XDK in chunks and sold it back repeatedly so each sell shrank the pair's XDK reserve, then sold the rest for the pair's GPC and swapped the GPC to WBNB.",
